    <briefdescription>
<para>Primary (terminal) template for the reflection mixin chain. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Serves as the empty base case of the <computeroutput>reflect</computeroutput> inheritance chain. <computeroutput>detail::wrapper</computeroutput> inherits (transitively) from this class; each partial specialisation for a concrete <computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> injects the proxy members generated by <computeroutput>SCL_REFLECT_METHOD</computeroutput> into the wrapper&apos;s public interface.</para>
<para>When <computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> matches no partial specialisation, this empty body is used — meaning no extra proxy members are added for that type.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Wrapper</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The outermost wrapper type that inherits this mixin. Used by <computeroutput>SCL_REFLECT_TYPE</computeroutput> to locate the executor at call time via <computeroutput><ref refid="structscl_1_1feature_1_1executor__trait" kindref="compound">scl::feature::executor_trait</ref>&lt;Wrapper&gt;</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Executor</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The outermost executor instantiation (<computeroutput>Executor&lt;Wrapper::value_type&gt;</computeroutput>). Exposed as <computeroutput>S_c_L_executor_type_</computeroutput> inside generated proxy methods. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Type</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type whose reflected members are mixed in. Partial specialisations handle <computeroutput>detail::wrapper</computeroutput> layers (delegating to the inner value type) and concrete value types (injecting proxy members). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
